===========================	Logs and Artifact

Artifacts are test-cases reports, logs Genrated data ,, and Artifacts keeps its data in  file for downloding for further discussion and R&D.
that is genrated from pipelines logs and reports.
Artifacts like: google drive, Jfrog, AWS Artifacts and GitLab have its own Artifacts

. project-settings ==> CICD ==> Artifacts ==> keep its checkbox ticked

Note: use this Artifacts in your pipeline. so have to define on stage onwhich you want artifacts
example:

test_job:
    stage: test
    script:
        - echo "This is testing of out docker build done by $CI_COMMIT_AUTHOR"
        - echo "these are my test results" > logs/app.log
    artifacts:
        paths:
            - logs/

